  "description": "While the new Wildcat 150 resembles our original shorter-travel bike, both aesthetically and in terms of suspension design, it is unique in that the front triangle has been completely redesigned to accommodate the new angles and geometry – namely a steeper seat tube and slacker head tube. And of course we’ve factored in a taller fork (571mm A to C) for 160mm of squish up front.\n\nThe new design produces different leverage and anti-squat ratios, but remains a very efficient pedaler.\n\nWe designed the suspension to be soft off the top for great small-bump compliance, and fairly progressive and linear throughout the rest of the travel.\n\nSo there you go, you’ve got MORE. Now go get after it.",
